Z||000000||Haze_Performance||11-24-2001||12:40 AM||||I have a file that I saved. <P>Fiero_84.14.Red<P>It asks what do I want to open it with.. Its a pic of a Fiero that I want to turn into a jpg or gif..  What do I open a "RED" with & how do I convert it?<P>Thank You<BR>-Haze  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR> <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/goodlife.gif">    <BR><FONT SIZE="1"><FONT COLOR="purple">Goto Website - <A HREF="http://www.ClassicFiero.com" TARGET=_blank>Click Here</A> </FONT></FONT>||||reg||5
Z||000001||maryjane||11-24-2001||12:51 AM||||Never heard of a .red file extension. I did a search at 2 file extension name sites, and it wasn't listed on either one. Did you try highlighting it and try to rename it as .jpg or even click on 'save as' then click on 'jpg.' If you want, email it to me (has to be under 400kb) and I will try to do something with it.<BR>Don<p>[This message has been edited by maryjane (edited 11-24-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Haze_Performance||11-24-2001||01:23 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by maryjane:<BR><B>Never heard of a .red file extension. I did a search at 2 file extension name sites, and it wasn't listed on either one. Did you try highlighting it and try to rename it as .jpg or even click on 'save as' then click on 'jpg.' If you want, email it to me (has to be under 400kb) and I will try to do something with it.<BR>Don<P>[This message has been edited by maryjane (edited 11-24-2001).]</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Thank You......... Its on the way...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>||||reg||14
Z||000003||Tigger||11-24-2001||02:01 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Haze_Performance:<BR><B>I have a file that I saved. <P>Fiero_84.14.Red</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Try removing the first "." most times programs will choke because it can't tell what kind of file it is.  Do what maryjane said, add .jpg or .gif at the end of it.  Might get lucky.<P>I've never seen a .red file.  There is a .ras which is a Sun Raster image file.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Haze_Performance||11-24-2001||02:06 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Tigger:<BR><B> Try removing the first "." most times programs will choke because it can't tell what kind of file it is.  Do what maryjane said, add .jpg or .gif at the end of it.  Might get lucky.<P>I've never seen a .red file.  There is a .ras which is a Sun Raster image file.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>There was no " in it.. its just Fiero_84.14.Red<P>I tried to add gif & jpg... No luck. I need to open it with something first..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><BR>||||reg||9
