Z||000006||Haze_Performance||11-24-2001||02:48 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by maryjane:<BR><B>I tried to rename it, tried to reassociate it, tried converting it. Best I came up with is the square witha red x. It's definitly an image file, when it asked what to use to open<BR>it with, I clicked on internet explorer, and it came right up as a red Fiero. I dunno. sorry</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Thanks anyhoo.... That pic came from <A HREF="http://www.tirerack.com" TARGET=_blank>www.tirerack.com</A>  . It's off the interactive wheel selector thingy.. I wanted to use it along with some of the tire pics on there. (also the same type of file) Oh well.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>||||reg||14
Z||000007||maryjane||11-24-2001||03:54 AM||||It was a bitmap. converted to jpg with scanner software.<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/red_fiero.jpg"> <BR>If you want different tires & wheels on it from that site, redownload it. Make sure you right click directly on the car. I didn't alter the setup when I captured it. It may be that when you change the wheels and tires in the picture, it changes the file extension. <p>[This message has been edited by maryjane (edited 11-24-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||Haze_Performance||11-24-2001||04:06 AM||||I just tried it... No luck. I have to copy the aftermarket wheel separately. What do I need to convert the wheels?||||reg||14
Z||000009||maryjane||11-24-2001||04:20 AM||||When you change from the stock to aftermarket wheels, it becomes the fiero_84.14.red file which actually shows up as a gif file. Like I said, with that you'll have to get someone smarter than me to do it.<BR>Probably download it as two different files and combine the parts in photoshop. That should be just about anybody on PFF. sorry<BR>Ok, I went back to it & changed the wheels & tires, but forgot which ones you wanted. Get your options set on the car, with tires & wheels. When you right click on the center of the car, the box should give you the option to 'save as'. click on it, and save it as bmp(bitmap). jpg isn't one of the options. Then open it with scanner or photo imaging soft ware and click save as jpg. Or email me all the options, and I will try it.<p>[This message has been edited by maryjane (edited 11-24-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000010||Nashco||11-24-2001||05:28 AM||||Easiest way to capture that image would be to hit the "print screen" button on your keyboard while viewing the web page.  Then go into Photoshop, open a new image, and "ctrl+v" (paste) the image into the new image file.  You should get a carbon copy of your previous desktop, and you can crop out the crap you don't want.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
